THIRD-PARTY NOTICES

This product includes software developed by third parties. The complete
list of direct and indirect dependencies is recorded in go.mod / go.sum,
and a machine-readable license report can be regenerated at any time
with `make security-licenses` (wrapping `go-licenses report ./...`).

The exhaustive list is in go.mod; the components below are called out
because they are significant to the runtime architecture or have
attribution requirements beyond the standard Apache-2.0 / MIT / BSD
permissive-license pattern.

Notable dependencies:

  Messaging + storage:
  - NATS server + Go client (Apache 2.0) - https://nats.io
  - etcd v3 (Apache 2.0) - https://etcd.io
  - modernc.org/sqlite (BSD-3-Clause Go port; underlying SQLite engine
    is public domain) - https://gitlab.com/cznic/sqlite

  Control-plane + observability:
  - gRPC (Apache 2.0) - https://grpc.io
  - OpenTelemetry Go (Apache 2.0) - https://opentelemetry.io
  - Prometheus client_golang (Apache 2.0) - https://github.com/prometheus/client_golang

  Identity + secrets:
  - SPIFFE go-spiffe (Apache 2.0) - https://spiffe.io
  - HashiCorp Vault API (Mozilla Public License 2.0) - https://www.vaultproject.io
    MPL-2.0 obligations apply to modifications of upstream source
    files; this project consumes Vault as a library client without
    modifying its source, so the MPL-2.0 attribution requirement is
    satisfied by referencing the upstream LICENSE. The same applies
    to the broader set of MPL-2.0 dependencies shipped with the
    binaries — Vault auth submodules (api/auth/approle,
    api/auth/kubernetes, api/auth/ldap), HashiCorp common utilities
    transitive to Vault (errwrap, go-cleanhttp, go-multierror,
    go-retryablehttp, go-rootcerts, go-secure-stdlib/parseutil,
    go-secure-stdlib/strutil, go-sockaddr, hcl), and the unrelated
    cyphar/filepath-securejoin. Each is enumerated with its
    canonical LICENSE link by `make security-licenses`.

  Policy + scripting:
  - OPA (Apache 2.0) - https://www.openpolicyagent.org
  - CEL (Apache 2.0) - https://github.com/google/cel-go
  - Starlark (BSD 3-Clause) - https://github.com/google/starlark-go

  GitOps + backup destinations:
  - go-git v5 (Apache 2.0) - https://github.com/go-git/go-git
  - minio-go v7 (Apache 2.0) - https://github.com/minio/minio-go

  Per Apache-2.0 §4, the NOTICE files of upstream Apache-2.0
  dependencies that ship their own NOTICE are honored by reference to
  their LICENSE+NOTICE files in their respective source repositories.
  The license-report tooling (`make security-licenses`) enumerates
  every direct and indirect dependency with a link to the canonical
  LICENSE on each project's upstream forge.

  One dependency, modernc.org/mathutil, reports as license "Unknown"
  in the automated scan; the upstream actually ships under BSD-3-Clause
  but in a non-standard layout that scanners don't recognize. The
  exception is tracked in docs/project/SECURITY-GOVERNANCE.md under
  "Dependency posture".
